Subject: [PATCH] Keep standalone host protoc and Abseil in the expected runtime layout

The Darwin cross build runs an ARM64 protoc while compiling Intel targets.
Its install RPATH searches protobuf/lib64, which already links to the standalone
build root's lib64 directory. Abseil previously stayed in abseil/absl instead,
so dyld aborted every protobuf generation command. Set the helper library's
output directory only in the IN_CROSS_COMPILE standalone project.

--- a/android/third_party/protobuf/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/android/third_party/protobuf/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -105,6 +105,12 @@
 # In the cross compile case we will have to make sure that what symlink the
 # lib64 directory
 if(IN_CROSS_COMPILE)
+  # This standalone host-tool build does not inherit the emulator's library
+  # output directory. Keep Abseil in the lib64 directory searched by protoc's
+  # install RPATH and the symlink below; otherwise the built host protoc cannot
+  # run while generating sources for the other architecture.
+  set_target_properties(abseil_dll PROPERTIES LIBRARY_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY
+                                            "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/lib64")
   execute_process(
     COMMAND
       ${CMAKE_COMMAND} -E create_symlink "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/lib64"
